Yes. In `buildResourceSlots`, if a slot’s id is already in `conflictsBySlotId`, it reuses that list and does **not** call `findFirstConflict` again:

```85:93:server/src/slots/slots.service.ts
      for (const slot of candidates) {
        const knownConflicts = conflictsBySlotId.get(slot.id);
        if (knownConflicts) {
          annotatedSlots.push({
            ...slot,
            conflicts: knownConflicts,
          });
          continue;
        }
```

That’s memoization for when the same slot shows up again (e.g. as a blocking resource’s slot on another resource’s candidate list). It skips recomputing conflicts; it does **not** drop the conflict — it still attaches the cached ones.

`applyKnownConflicts` at the end does another pass so any later-discovered conflicts get written onto earlier annotations too.
